			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Correct import path for URI normalization utility\n\nResolve a broken import path in `Source/IPC/WindServiceHandlers/Extensions.rs` where the `Normalize` module was referenced incorrectly. Update the path from `IPC::UriComponents::Normalize` to `IPC::UriComponents::Normalize::Fn` to align with the actual module structure and expose the normalization function required for processing extension URIs.\n\nThis ensures the extension management handlers can correctly resolve URI components during the filtering of installed extensions, preventing potential runtime panics or logic errors when interacting with the `Wind` service layer.",
			"SHA": "27f727498c52bb68469eda25b9df43e452c463e8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T09:06:51Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1191,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Common): Introduce health monitoring data models and score logic\n\nDefine the core data structures for the editor's health monitoring subsystem within `Source/IPC/Common/HealthStatus`. This commit adds `SeverityLevel::Enum` to classify issue criticality, `HealthIssue::Enum` as a tagged union for specific failure modes (e.g., MemoryPressure, ConnectionLoss), and `HealthMonitor::Struct` to aggregate state.\n\nThe `HealthMonitor` calculates a dynamic `HealthScore` (0-100) based on a deterministic penalty system derived from issue severities (Low: -5, Medium: -15, High: -25, Critical: -40). It provides methods for adding/removing issues, filtering by severity, and determining overall system health status (`IsHealthy`, `IsCritical`). All types derive `Serialize`/`Deserialize` to enable transmission over the gRPC (Vine) and Tauri IPC channels for real-time status propagation to the Wind and Sky layers.\n\nThese models lay the foundation for the backend to expose service liveness metrics to the frontend without blocking the main thread.",
			"SHA": "23d6eddefce6d663ef87fdd01e468309c773f80d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T09:06:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1187,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement LSP command stubs for code intelligence\n\nIntroduce a suite of new Tauri commands under `Source/Command/LanguageFeature` to expose core language server protocol capabilities to the Wind service layer. These commands act as the IPC bridge for code actions, completions, go-to-definition, document highlights, hover information, and reference finding.\n\nEach command (`MountainProvideCodeActions`, `MountainProvideCompletions`, `MountainProvideDefinition`, `MountainProvideDocumentHighlights`, `MountainProvideHover`, `MountainProvideReferences`) adheres to the project's PascalCase naming convention and delegates execution to the corresponding concrete implementation within `Command::LanguageFeature::<Feature>::provide_<feature>_impl`. The functions accept document URIs, cursor positions, and context payloads as JSON `Value` types, deferring strict deserialization to the downstream implementation logic to ensure a flexible interface during early development.\n\nThis commit expands the backend's LSP surface area, enabling the frontend to request and render intelligent coding assistance features without blocking the main thread.",
			"SHA": "17c441b85904b7aac47fecdcfd0150b57ac56ca0"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T09:06:25Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1181,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Define hover command data models and DTOs\n\nIntroduce the foundational data structures for the Hover subsystem within `Source/Command/Hover/Interface`. This commit establishes the contract for LSP-compatible hover requests and responses, adhering to the project's strict PascalCase naming conventions.\n\nThe implementation adds:\n- `Position::Struct`: Zero-based line and character offset.\n- `Range::Struct`: Inclusive range bounded by start/end positions.\n- `HoverRequest::Struct`: Inbound DTO capturing document URI and cursor position.\n- `HoverContent::Enum`: Tagged union for plain text, markdown, and markup with language hints.\n- `HoverResponse::Struct`: Outbound DTO containing an ordered list of content items and an optional range.\n\nAll types derive `Serialize` and `Deserialize` to enable JSON transmission over the Tauri IPC event bus. These models prepare the `Wind` service layer to request and render code documentation overlays without blocking the main thread.",
			"SHA": "8c97e9610fb18bcb7c930ab071089290d80aab28"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T09:06:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1175,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Introduce test provider state and lifecycle data models\n\nEstablish the foundational data structures for the testing subsystem within the `Source/Environment/TestProvider` module. This commit introduces five new types adhering to project PascalCase conventions:\n\n- `TestControllerState::Struct`: Registration record for extension-provided controllers.\n- `TestProviderState::Struct`: Aggregate state managing controller registries and active run maps.\n- `TestRun::Struct`: Active execution context tracking status, timing, and per-test results.\n- `TestResult::Struct`: Per-test outcome including pass/fail status, duration, and failure diagnostics.\n- `TestRunStatus::Enum`: Lifecycle state machine (Queued, Running, Passed, Failed, Skipped, Errored).\n\nThese types utilize `Serialize`/`Deserialize` traits for IPC readiness and are designed to be held behind `tokio::sync::RwLock` in `ApplicationState` for concurrent access during test execution. This lays the groundwork for the `Wind` service layer to manage test discovery, execution, and reporting without blocking the main thread.",
			"SHA": "8b4bbfdf16647ae11cc85575c822c7f60d75f7a0"
		}
	],
